<p>Australian authorities have arrested former SAS soldier and Victoria Cross recipient Ben Roberts-Smith over alleged war crimes during deployments in Afghanistan between 2009 and 2012. Police said he faces five charges tied to the alleged killings of five Afghan civilians: two counts of murder and three counts of aiding or abetting murder. Each charge carries a maximum sentence of life imprisonment. Roberts-Smith has consistently denied wrongdoing and has not yet entered a plea. At a Sydney hearing on Wednesday, Roberts-Smith remained in custody after his legal team did not seek bail. The case will return to court for a bail review on 17 April. The charges follow a lengthy federal police investigation and come after a 2023 civil defamation ruling found substantial truth in newspaper reports that he committed unlawful killings in Afghanistan. Legal experts say the case could become an important test of Australia’s willingness and ability to prosecute alleged war crimes committed overseas under its own laws.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/mS_spSw9Vc1SwiGcE8LEgG9yFg4SImCpK8-In9ezJtMdkC4XeMmRbZa1ID0FlJVGjbsMbT0yUlhQ4KB_ANPlZgrS8vW1lVNJlwS5_VNnDfSrkDzdoy3J9C5g4IaryOJkwgP6CzTu9z-7SblgUXCSJSlMiSrkikqCujIq-NjFkA' alt='Ben Roberts-Smith appears in reporting on the Sydney war crimes case.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Alleged victims: AFP Commissioner Krissy Barrett said prosecutors will argue the victims were detained, unarmed and not taking part in hostilities when they were killed.</li><li>Rare prosecution: Former Human Rights Commission president Gillian Triggs said a criminal trial over alleged battlefield offences abroad would be almost unheard of in modern Australian practice.</li><li>Public support: Mining billionaire Gina Rinehart publicly questioned the justification for the prosecution, showing that some high-profile support for Roberts-Smith remains.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Australian Federal Police: Police say the case centers on allegations that Afghan civilians were killed while detained and under Australian Defence Force control, framing it as a war crimes prosecution rather than a dispute over battlefield casualties. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637591-australian-soldier-arrested-war-crimes-afghanistan/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Gillian Triggs: The former Australian Human Rights Commission president said the case will draw international attention because Australia has very few modern precedents for prosecuting alleged war crimes committed overseas. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/roberts-smith-to-front-court-after-night-spent-in-cell/'>Michael West</a>)</li><li>Ben Roberts-Smith and his legal team: Roberts-Smith continues to deny the allegations, and his lawyers did not immediately seek bail at Wednesday’s hearing, leaving him in custody pending a later review. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/apr/08/ben-roberts-smith-court-news-war-crimes-charges-silverwater-jail-ntwnfb'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Gina Rinehart: Rinehart questioned the time and public cost spent investigating former soldiers, reflecting a strand of support that views the prosecution skeptically. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/apr/08/ben-roberts-smith-brs-gina-rinehart-alleged-war-crimes-arrest-ntwnfb'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637591-australian-soldier-arrested-war-crimes-afghanistan/'>One of Australia’s most-decorated soldiers arrested on war crimes charges</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/roberts-smith-to-front-court-after-night-spent-in-cell/'>Roberts-Smith to front court after night spent in cell</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/apr/08/ben-roberts-smith-court-news-war-crimes-charges-silverwater-jail-ntwnfb'>Ben Roberts-Smith to remain in jail after bail hearing over war crimes charges</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/decorated-australian-veteran-remains-bars-afghan-war-crime-131825638'>Decorated Australian veteran remains behind bars on Afghan war crime charges</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-07-0700/criminal-justice-authorities-arrest-countrys-most-decorated-soldier-over-alleged-war-crimes'>Authorities Arrest Country&#x27;s Most Decorated Soldier Over Alleged War Crimes</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/former-australian-soldier-remain-jail-after-being-charged-afghan-war-crimes'>Former Australian soldier to remain in jail after being charged with Afghan war crimes</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/australias-most-decorated-soldier-ben-roberts-smith-arrested-over-alleged-war-2026-04-07/'>Australian Army veteran and Victoria Cross recipient Ben Roberts-Smith is arrested by police at Sydney Airport for alleged war crimes committed between 2009 and 2012 during his deployment to  Afghanistan.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>